      "message": "Thanks for the discussion today! Here\u0027s a working version of the front end cache, let me know what you think.\n\nSome thoughts on this approach:\n\n - I\u0027m not a big fan of having the view creation happen in a lambda, but the alternative was a fair amount of new plumbing between the Texture/TextureView/Device.\n - My initial inclination was to not add the new virtual call to RefCountedWithExternalCount due to the concerns Corentin mentioned, but I realized that the alternative was to require all the Texture backend impls to handle an `enableViewCache` constructor arg, which felt potentially confusing and error prone.\n - An alternative to that and the current approach is to add a TextureDescriptor chain struct that specifies that view caching should be enabled, which is then injected by the `APICreateTexture` call (or something around there). Less plumbing, but still feels potentially error prone and adds something that looks like API surface but is really only intended for internal use.",
